<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Richard Óg de Burgh, 2nd Earl of Ulster</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1259–1326</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Red Earl of Ulster</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Richard de Burgh, known as the Red Earl, was earl of Ulster and lord of Connacht, the most powerful Anglo-Norman lord in Ireland around 1300. He was overlord of the O'Neills, built castles such as Ballymote and Northburgh and fought for Edward I in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>. His daughter Elizabeth married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-the-bruce">Robert the Bruce</a>, whose brother Edward invaded Ireland in 1315.</p></div>
